      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a preliminary impact report for a new CTA transit extension project in chicago. i need to get a sense of how the new lines might affect different areas. i've got some district data here:\n\nDistrict A (near Lincoln Park): 75% White, 15% Hispanic, 5% Black, 5% Other.\nDistrict B (near Logan Square): 40% White, 45% Hispanic, 10% Black, 5% Other.\nDistrict C (near Bronzeville): 10% White, 15% Hispanic, 70% Black, 5% Other.\nDistrict D (near Englewood): 5% White, 10% Hispanic, 80% Black, 5% Other.\n\nbased on the current demographics and general urban trends, which of these areas do you think are most likely to see rapid gentrification/value spikes, and which ones might face more instability or potential decline in property values after the transit is built?",
